  "answer_text": "There are three common ways to calculate or convert grades into percentages. Choose the method below that matches your needs, or **reply with your scores/grades and I will calculate them for you!**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Points Score to Percentage (Test / Homework Grades)\nIf you have a specific score (e.g., you got 18 out of 23 on a test), use this formula:\n\n$$\\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Points Earned}}{\\text{Total Possible Points}} \\right) \\times 100$$\n\n*   **Example:** If you scored **41 out of 50**:\n    $$\\left( \\frac{41}{50} \\right) \\times 100 = 0.82 \\times 100 = 82\\%$$\n\n---\n\n### 2. Letter Grade to Percentage Converter\nThis table shows the standard US academic grading scale used to convert letter grades to their average percentage equivalents:\n\n| Letter Grade | Percentage Range | Midpoint (Average) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **A+** | 97% \u2013 100% | 98.5% |\n| **A** | 93% \u2013 96% | 94.5% |\n| **A-** | 90% \u2013 92% | 91% |\n| **B+** | 87% \u2013 89% | 88% |\n| **B** | 83% \u2013 86% | 84.5% |\n| **B-** | 80% \u2013 82% | 81% |\n| **C+** | 77% \u2013 79% | 78% |\n| **C** | 73% \u2013 76% | 74.5% |\n| **C-** | 70% \u2013 72% | 71% |\n| **D+** | 67% \u2013 69% | 68% |\n| **D** | 65% \u2013 66% | 65.5% |\n| **F** | Below 65% | 0% \u2013 64% |\n\n---\n\n### 3. GPA (4.0 Scale) to Percentage Converter\nIf you want to convert your cumulative Grade Point Average (GPA) into an overall percentage, the standard conversion formula is:\n\n$$\\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{GPA}}{4.0} \\right) \\times 100$$\n\nHere is a quick reference table for common GPA scores:\n\n| GPA (4.0 Scale) | Equivalent Percentage | Equivalent Letter Grade |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **4.0** | 95% \u2013 100% | A / A+ |\n| **3.7** | 90% \u2013 93% | A- |\n| **3.3** | 87% \u2013 89% | B+ |\n| **3.0** | 83% \u2013 86% | B |\n| **2.7** | 80% \u2013 82% | B- |\n| **2.3** | 77% \u2013 79% | C+ |\n| **2.0** | 73% \u2013 76% | C |\n| **1.7** | 70% \u2013 72% | C- |\n| **1.3** | 67% \u2013 69% | D+ |\n| **1.0** | 65% \u2013 66% | D |\n| **0.0** | Below 65% | F |\n\n---\n\n**Want me to calculate it for you?** \nJust reply with your numbers (for example: *\"I got 34 out of 45\"* or *\"My GPA is 3.4\"*) and I'll give you the exact percentage right away!",
